A define called from pre-line keeps its line-break count, even when an
earlier raw-text element holds a byte that is not UTF-8 (fuzz,
2026-11-03). A browser decodes the byte as U+FFFD and closes the
<textarea>; the template parser must close it too, or the call site
after it is not seen and the body's blank lines collapse.
-- input.gohtml --
{{define "m"}}
a


c
{{end}}
<textarea>è</textarea>
{{define "k"}}<div style="white-space:pre-line">{{template "m" .}}</div>{{end}}
-- format.gohtml --
{{define "m"}}
a


c
{{end}}
<textarea>è</textarea>
{{define "k"}}<div style="white-space:pre-line">{{template "m" .}}</div>{{end}}
